  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.3.0: Response caching. UseResponseCaching() serves repeat GET/HEAD requests from a bounded in-process store, skipping endpoint execution and JSON serialization, and emits Cache-Control/Vary/Age for client and proxy caches. Opt-in per endpoint via [ResponseCache(Duration, Location, VaryByHeader, VaryByQueryKeys)]. Entries expire on their duration and are evicted when a successful POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE hits the same path. Cache hits answer If-None-Match with 304 on HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3. Requests carrying Authorization bypass the shared cache unless the endpoint opts in. Also fixes HTTP/2 outbound flow control: the send path now honors the peer's stream- and connection-level send windows (RFC 7540 6.9) instead of queueing whole bodies at once, and the connection send window starts at the RFC default of 65535 with the client's SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE tracked separately.",
